+The policy target has no SQLite, filesystem, crypto, clock, or mutator
+dependency. It accepts already loaded durable queue facts and validates the
+relationships needed to mint action authority:
+
+- queue kind agrees with persisted state, ownership, expiry, retry window, and
+  terminal-review evidence;
+- chunk ranges are nonempty and overflow-safe;
+- mutating rows carry exact SHA-256-shaped request, schedule, execution, and
+  worker-lease authority keys;
+- terminal-review rows remain observable even when their historical mutation
+  key material is malformed; and
+- one execution idempotency key cannot mix mutation kinds.
+
+Terminal review has the highest priority. Mutation groups remain atomic under a
+bounded pass, observations remain singleton groups, and a deferred
+higher-priority group forms a barrier that lower-priority work cannot bypass to
+fill the action cap.
+
+The executor does not merely trust adjacent policy output. It independently
+checks contiguous action priorities, contiguous and complete groups, consistent
+group size/kind/mutation/key metadata, and exact returned-group counts before
+any mutation filter is built.
